WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:08.300
Storytelling is so important
for the human experience.

00:00:09.635 --> 00:00:14.181
Storytelling is a way to live hundreds
and thousands of lives in our lifetime.

00:00:15.516 --> 00:00:17.935
What I think is meaningful
about what we do is,

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:22.105
I can tell you a story that acknowledges
you as a human being a little bit,

00:00:22.189 --> 00:00:25.067
and you take my worldview
with you when you walk out.

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.945
We both get something
out of that, in a beautiful way.

00:00:36.119 --> 00:00:39.414
What I think is really powerful
about long-form storytelling

00:00:39.498 --> 00:00:43.335
is that you can really dig deeper
and excavate and unfold things

00:00:43.418 --> 00:00:45.045
that enrich the whole story

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:50.676
But there’s always the fear
that you’ll never get to finish it,

00:00:50.759 --> 00:00:52.386
never get to tell the end of the story.

00:00:52.469 --> 00:00:55.013
I think that’s one of the things
that scared me the most

00:00:55.097 --> 00:00:57.391
about going into long-form television.

00:00:57.474 --> 00:00:59.309
-Here we go.
-And background.

00:00:59.393 --> 00:01:00.269
And action!

00:01:00.352 --> 00:01:02.980
It’s five hours of material every year.

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:04.857
That’s two and a half movies.

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:07.150
It takes me two years to make one film.

00:01:07.234 --> 00:01:09.152
And cut! Excellent.

00:01:09.236 --> 00:01:12.197
I’m so grateful
that we had this opportunity

00:01:12.281 --> 00:01:15.158
and that we got to finish the story.

00:01:15.242 --> 00:01:16.869
Beautiful.

00:01:16.952 --> 00:01:20.205
When we started it, we knew the premise
and we knew the two storylines,

00:01:20.289 --> 00:01:22.124
but we really didn’t know
where it was going to go.

00:01:22.207 --> 00:01:25.627
And then, by the end of that first season,
it started to become clear.

00:01:26.003 --> 00:01:29.923
Do you know who you welcomed
into your home?

00:01:30.132 --> 00:01:32.509
When the pandemic hiatused us,

00:01:32.593 --> 00:01:36.889
it was a real moment, that was kind of
beautiful, for me to sit down and go,

00:01:36.972 --> 00:01:39.808
“Okay, these are all the different
ideas that we have.

00:01:39.892 --> 00:01:42.352
How many seasons is that?
How many episodes is that?”

00:01:42.436 --> 00:01:45.147
That was how it kind of came
to be a four-season show.

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:46.773
You're getting more clarity.

00:01:47.691 --> 00:01:50.569
My name is Leanne Grayson,
and I come from Wisconsin.

00:01:51.403 --> 00:01:57.075
One of the fun ideas for the show
was telling the origin story of Leanne.

00:01:58.202 --> 00:02:00.412
It can be interpreted in two ways.

00:02:00.495 --> 00:02:07.085
Is this the story of a fallen angel,
embodied now in this young girl?

00:02:07.586 --> 00:02:11.924
As she embraces this,
does she become this dark entity

00:02:12.007 --> 00:02:14.968
that could really change
the balance of everything?

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:22.809
Or is this just a girl
that has these delusions,

00:02:22.893 --> 00:02:25.729
and maybe there’s a grounded explanation?

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:27.523
Why would she put
her own baby in your crib?

00:02:28.774 --> 00:02:30.526
Both explanations are plausible.

00:02:30.609 --> 00:02:32.736
That’s a fun story that we wanted to tell.

00:02:34.947 --> 00:02:35.781
Ah!

00:02:38.283 --> 00:02:40.619
One of the hopes
when I hired Nell Tiger Free

00:02:40.702 --> 00:02:42.746
was that we would watch this young girl

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:45.916
grow into a woman
over the course of the show.

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:48.252
And then,
when we get to the final season,

00:02:48.335 --> 00:02:50.712
she would be a formidable presence.

00:02:50.796 --> 00:02:51.797
Do you think I’m scary?

00:02:57.094 --> 00:02:58.720
What about now?

00:02:58.804 --> 00:03:00.722
I love that architecture for her.

00:03:00.889 --> 00:03:02.015
What about now?

00:03:06.228 --> 00:03:09.231
Ultimately, what drew her
to this house is Dorothy.

00:03:09.606 --> 00:03:11.942
She’s just in awe of Dorothy.

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:16.363
Her need for Dorothy to accept her,
and love her, is primal.

00:03:16.446 --> 00:03:19.408
It’s a mother figure that she never had.

00:03:19.491 --> 00:03:21.368
Shhh. Shh. Shh.

00:03:21.451 --> 00:03:24.955
At first, it was longing
and doing the childlike things

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:26.373
but then getting more physical.

00:03:31.086 --> 00:03:33.755
She’s so tired of feeling bad,
and feeling wrong,

00:03:33.839 --> 00:03:35.757
and feeling like she isn’t good enough.

00:03:37.384 --> 00:03:39.303
Which is all the dynamics
from her real mom.

00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:42.306
She’s started to feel it again
with this family,

00:03:44.266 --> 00:03:45.809
and she’s not going to have it.

00:03:45.976 --> 00:03:47.519
You should all be very careful.

00:03:48.896 --> 00:03:51.023
Now she sees the fear in their eyes.

00:03:51.607 --> 00:03:53.317
She likes this feeling.

00:03:53.984 --> 00:03:55.444
She starts to get to the premise of,

00:03:55.527 --> 00:03:57.487
"I need to get everything
out of this house

00:03:57.571 --> 00:03:59.489
except for me and Dorothy
and this child."

00:04:00.949 --> 00:04:03.243
I’m never gonna let you
back in this house.

00:04:03.911 --> 00:04:08.040
Eventually, Dorothy will come to see
that this is a good thing.

00:04:09.291 --> 00:04:10.542
That’s her fantasy.

00:04:10.626 --> 00:04:13.420
She’s going to do everything possible
to make that happen.

00:04:13.504 --> 00:04:15.130
It’s just you and me now.

00:04:16.048 --> 00:04:18.884
Just let me take my child and leave!

00:04:20.135 --> 00:04:25.724
Jericho has always been the embodiment
of love, and fragility and vulnerability,

00:04:25.807 --> 00:04:28.977
that represents all of our hopes
and fears when we have a kid,

00:04:29.061 --> 00:04:32.564
and whether we’re going to fail
or succeed in protecting them.

00:04:33.065 --> 00:04:35.359
And the helplessness that we all feel.

00:04:35.692 --> 00:04:37.110
That’s so scary.

00:04:41.073 --> 00:04:45.494
Whenever we see Jericho as he’s moving
through the developmental stages,

00:04:45.577 --> 00:04:47.829
like his birthday,
and he’s learning to eat,

00:04:47.913 --> 00:04:49.206
each of these things.

00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:52.543
This is the treasure
that’s being given this family.

00:04:52.626 --> 00:04:57.798
Every time they hold him, it feels
like it’s worth it, whatever the cost is.

00:05:03.804 --> 00:05:07.558
Servant is about a woman
who’s forgotten that she was responsible

00:05:07.641 --> 00:05:10.143
for her child’s death,
and the ticking clock

00:05:10.227 --> 00:05:12.187
about when she’s going to remember.

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:17.776
That’s why I did this show.
I wanted to get to that episode.

00:05:18.944 --> 00:05:20.445
Her story was so important.

00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:23.490
I wanted to direct
her descent into madness,

00:05:23.574 --> 00:05:25.617
and I wanted to direct
the moment she woke up.

00:05:25.951 --> 00:05:27.786
Ahhhhh!

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:30.372
We’re all fighting not to have
that painful moment,

00:05:30.455 --> 00:05:33.834
but the irony is, that’s exactly
the moment we should all be running to.

00:05:33.917 --> 00:05:35.544
It was a freak accident.

00:05:35.627 --> 00:05:40.174
The thing that we’re scared to say,
for fear that,

00:05:40.257 --> 00:05:42.467
"I don’t know what’s going
to happen on the other side."

00:05:42.759 --> 00:05:45.012
That’s very much human nature.

00:05:49.516 --> 00:05:53.145
I always try to put myself in the mindset
of the characters and say,

00:05:53.228 --> 00:05:55.147
"Would I do this?”

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:57.941
There is no higher stakes
than losing your child,

00:05:58.525 --> 00:06:02.154
having the person you love
disappear in front of your eyes.

00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:06.325
I would probably do anything
to get back what I had lost.

00:06:08.243 --> 00:06:10.996
Sean has made a Faustian bargain,

00:06:11.496 --> 00:06:15.292
and realizes that
there’s no way out of this.

00:06:15.375 --> 00:06:17.211
You’ve already made your choice.

00:06:18.712 --> 00:06:21.215
So be an adult and deal
with the consequences.

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:27.012
It’s coming at a cost, and the cost is,

00:06:27.095 --> 00:06:30.098
he doesn’t get to talk about
what happened to them and the loss.

00:06:30.807 --> 00:06:33.352
You should have been there, Julian.
She called you!

00:06:33.519 --> 00:06:34.978
But we’re not ready
to talk about that, are we?

00:06:35.062 --> 00:06:38.106
And we’ll never be ready,
because you can’t handle real life.

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:40.234
One inconvenience,
and you fall off the wagon.

00:06:40.317 --> 00:06:41.985
Julian is an addict,

00:06:42.069 --> 00:06:46.907
and keeps on doing forms of addiction,
whether it’s drugs or materialism.

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:51.036
He’ll do anything to escape
the feeling of guilt and trauma

00:06:51.119 --> 00:06:54.122
that has associated with the events
that happened to this family.

00:06:55.624 --> 00:06:56.458
Sean!

00:06:57.584 --> 00:06:58.418
Julian!

00:06:59.169 --> 00:07:02.548
There’s a pretty dark moment
where Sean and Julian

00:07:02.631 --> 00:07:06.802
come to the realization
that this girl has to leave this house.

00:07:08.387 --> 00:07:10.597
We’re going to stop being polite.

00:07:11.056 --> 00:07:13.225
We may have to cross the line here.

00:07:15.477 --> 00:07:16.812
Hello, Leanne.

00:07:16.895 --> 00:07:18.564
It’s shocking to all of them.

00:07:19.523 --> 00:07:20.732
They’re questioning themselves.

00:07:20.816 --> 00:07:24.945
Wow, when we’re fighting for our family,
we are willing to hurt someone else.

00:07:27.447 --> 00:07:30.909
That’s what scary about having
a darker presence near you.

00:07:30.993 --> 00:07:34.371
You start to take on
all of their value systems.

00:07:34.454 --> 00:07:37.708
They're like, “See, you’d do anything,
too, to get what you want.”

00:07:39.209 --> 00:07:42.171
I’m so sorry for what we did to you.

00:07:43.714 --> 00:07:45.799
It is primarily these four actors,

00:07:45.883 --> 00:07:48.677
constantly interacting
for these 40 episodes.

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:50.929
It is a play, essentially.

00:07:52.764 --> 00:07:55.851
They were game for what I was
asking them to do, which is,

00:07:55.934 --> 00:07:58.770
“Hey, we’re going to push
the artistic mediums.

00:07:59.938 --> 00:08:02.024
We’re going to shoot
these things in unusual ways,

00:08:02.107 --> 00:08:04.985
and sometimes it’s not going to work,
but we’re going to keep pushing it.”

00:08:05.068 --> 00:08:09.615
And they were so open to risk themselves,
rather than play it safe.

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:12.451
I think they found it exciting

00:08:12.534 --> 00:08:16.205
to be risking themselves
in that way for those 40 episodes.

00:08:18.874 --> 00:08:23.253
I’m prepared to do whatever it takes
to get rid of Leanne.

00:08:24.671 --> 00:08:26.131
The biblical story that we’re telling

00:08:26.215 --> 00:08:29.134
is being manifested
in physical form in the house.

00:08:30.719 --> 00:08:33.889
The house has always been
a reflection of the family.

00:08:33.972 --> 00:08:35.974
As the house is deteriorating,

00:08:36.058 --> 00:08:37.851
it’s almost like
you’re in your own nightmare,

00:08:37.935 --> 00:08:41.271
and you start to sense
that this is not sustainable.

00:08:43.023 --> 00:08:44.733
Now, this has escalated to the point

00:08:44.816 --> 00:08:48.320
that we’re on the cusp
of something catastrophic.

00:08:48.946 --> 00:08:54.743
If she wins, the city will fall,
and that’s only the beginning.

00:08:57.621 --> 00:09:01.750
The last episode is reducing
all 40 episodes

00:09:01.834 --> 00:09:06.922
to the primal conversation of a mom
who didn’t get a chance to mother,

00:09:07.005 --> 00:09:11.009
and a child who didn’t have
a mother to mother her.

00:09:12.511 --> 00:09:15.013
Will they be able to find balance?

00:09:15.097 --> 00:09:17.766
And if they can’t,
everything is going to fall apart.

00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:19.935
Not only what’s in the house,
but the whole world.

00:09:20.018 --> 00:09:24.147
A world out of balance
is a world of endless suffering,

00:09:24.231 --> 00:09:27.609
unless you choose to end it.

00:09:27.693 --> 00:09:31.071
Ultimately, Leanne has to make
a very difficult choice

00:09:31.154 --> 00:09:33.866
to help this family and the world.

00:09:34.867 --> 00:09:38.745
It’s a beautiful thing, that the domestic
story of a shattered family

00:09:38.829 --> 00:09:42.291
and this biblical story
of this dark entity

00:09:42.374 --> 00:09:44.877
meet in this storyline
of a mother and a daughter.

00:09:49.965 --> 00:09:52.384
What was really interesting,
when I look back on it,

00:09:52.467 --> 00:09:56.972
because I didn’t think of it
as my story only,

00:09:57.055 --> 00:10:00.350
there was a little bit
of distance that I had from it

00:10:00.434 --> 00:10:05.439
that allowed me to be very loose
with my storytelling,

00:10:05.522 --> 00:10:07.774
in a way that I’ve never been able to do.

00:10:07.858 --> 00:10:11.320
I felt, to some extent,
I was following the muse in my head.

00:10:11.403 --> 00:10:16.033
I had all these amazing writers
and directors to help tell the story.

00:10:16.491 --> 00:10:20.412
I got to work with an incredible
group of storytellers

00:10:20.495 --> 00:10:24.333
that I normally wouldn’t have gotten
a chance to tell stories with.

00:10:25.709 --> 00:10:28.879
You will distinctly feel
each filmmaker’s hands,

00:10:28.962 --> 00:10:32.883
and why episode 401
is really different than the second one,

00:10:32.966 --> 00:10:35.636
which is really different
than the third episode.

00:10:35.719 --> 00:10:37.679
And they’re very different
than my episode,

00:10:37.763 --> 00:10:40.974
but it’s all one family of language.

00:10:41.058 --> 00:10:44.937
And I do think celebrating
our differences in our voices and artistry

00:10:45.020 --> 00:10:48.357
will make Servant have deep,
deep resonance.

00:10:48.732 --> 00:10:53.403
It’s 40 little films that were directed
by these incredible storytellers.

00:10:54.071 --> 00:10:54.988
-And cut!
-Cutting.

00:10:55.072 --> 00:10:56.156
All right, great. Check it.

00:10:57.324 --> 00:11:01.745
Servant, I think, forever will be
a magical experience for me.

00:11:01.828 --> 00:11:08.377
It is something that we had got to do
with such purity, in such an unusual way.

00:11:10.003 --> 00:11:11.755
When we got to the last episode,

00:11:11.839 --> 00:11:15.008
and we said goodbye
to the cast and the crew,

00:11:15.092 --> 00:11:18.554
it was super emotional,
because we know this is rare.

00:11:18.637 --> 00:11:21.348
To have this much love
and artistic integrity

00:11:21.431 --> 00:11:23.809
in something, in the industry,
is very, very rare.

00:11:23.892 --> 00:11:25.727
-And cut!
-Cutting.

00:11:28.856 --> 00:11:31.942
I just wanted to thank you guys
for everything.

00:11:32.025 --> 00:11:36.613
I got to do this in a way, with people
I love, at the highest level,

00:11:36.697 --> 00:11:38.949
and, you guys, you just…
I just can’t thank you enough.

00:11:39.032 --> 00:11:42.327
It'll always be one of my most
cherished memories.

00:11:42.411 --> 00:11:45.539
And I want to thank my amazing cast.

00:11:50.294 --> 00:11:51.837
Love you all. You’re all family.

00:11:58.093 --> 00:12:02.389
I went to the set for the very last time,
and I stood there and looked around.

00:12:02.472 --> 00:12:04.141
I did take one or two pictures.

00:12:05.684 --> 00:12:08.562
The set's getting torn down.
It’ll never exist.

00:12:08.645 --> 00:12:10.480
We’ll never tell that story again.

00:12:11.857 --> 00:12:15.444
I know one day I’m going
to be walking and just start weeping,

00:12:16.570 --> 00:12:19.281
because I don’t know
how it could happen again,

00:12:19.364 --> 00:12:21.617
to have that magic that bonded us all.

00:12:22.826 --> 00:12:27.581
My hope is that Servant
will be watched for years to come.

00:12:28.498 --> 00:12:30.918
I want it to be meaningful
and stick with you.

00:12:32.294 --> 00:12:35.088
Having had this
artistically pure experience,

00:12:35.172 --> 00:12:38.383
that Apple allowed me to have,
I’m so grateful.

